<%- include('partials/header') %>
        <section>
            <h2>About NetGuard</h2>
            <p>
                NetGuard was created to help everyday users understand the security
                of their Wi-Fi networks. Many people don't realize their home network
                may be vulnerable to unauthorized access.
            </p>
            <p>
                This tool asks a few simple questions and gives you a clear risk score
                with actionable steps to improve your security.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <article>
                <h3>How does NetGuard calculate my risk score?</h3>
                <p>
                    Each of the 10 answers is checked on the server. Every secure answer earns a point:
                    8–10 is Low risk, 5–7 is Medium, and 0–4 is High. Anything flagged is added to your checklist.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>Is my information saved?</h3>
                <p>
                    Your assessment results are saved on the NetGuard server so you can revisit them later
                    under "My Past Results". They are tied to an anonymous cookie in your browser — we don't
                    ask for your name, email or Wi-Fi details — and you can delete any result at any time.
                    Messages sent through the Contact form are stored so our team can reply.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>What should I do if I get a High Risk score?</h3>
                <p>
                    Follow the checklist provided. Start with changing your Wi-Fi
                    password and updating your router's firmware.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
